{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[(-5x+6)^5\\right]$ is the *second derivative* of $(-5x+6)^5$. In other words, it's the derivative of $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[(-5x+6)^5\\right]$, which is the derivative of $(-5x+6)^5$.\n\nBecause of this, we need to differentiate $(-5x+6)^5$ twice in order to find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[(-5x+6)^5\\right]$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[(-5x+6)^5\\right]$:\n\n$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[(-5x+6)^5\\right]=-25(-5x+6)^4$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[(-5x+6)^5\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5(-5x+6)^4\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}(-5x+6)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5(-5x+6)^4\\cdot(-5)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-25(-5x+6)^4\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $-25(-5x+6)^4$ to find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[(2x+1)^5\\right]$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[(-5x+6)^5\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-25(-5x+6)^4\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=500(-5x+6)^3\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[(-5x+6)^5\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-25(-5x+6)^4\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-25\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[(-5x+6)^4\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-25\\left(4(-5x+6)^3\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}(-5x+6)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-100(-5x+6)^3\\cdot(-5)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=500(-5x+6)^3\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[(-5x+6)^5\\right]=500(-5x+6)^3$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[(-5x+6)^5\\right]$.**\n\n[[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":"0","simplify":false,"value":"500(-5x+6)^{3}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"static":false,"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
